 Requirements', 'Admin Control Rule', 'Evidence Integrity Rule')\n- spot-check at least three file paths cited in 05 by reading them under v2/backend/app/domain/ to verify the cited symbol exists in the cited file.\n\nReview rubric. For each rubric item, record PASS / FAIL / WARN with evidence pointers (file path and section heading or line range).\n\n1. Chain-stage coverage. Every stage from REQ_0009's 'Required explanation chains' is represented in 05 'Per-stage chain inventory'. The 13 stages are: raw source data, feature snapshot construction, feature change detection, trainer prediction emission, confidence change packaging, signal emission, orchestrator decision, risk gateway decision, execution intent issuance, paper trader action, shadow trader action, live-blocked trader action, result/PnL attribution.\n\n2. Evidence integrity. Every claim of V2 ownership cites BOTH a file path under v2/backend/app/domain/ AND a specific exported symbol name (class/function/constant). Spot-check three rows: open the cited file, confirm the cited symbol exists. Discrepancies are FAIL.\n\n3. ID forwarding contract completeness. The 'ID forwarding contract' table covers all six ids REQ_0009 requires: feature_snapshot_id, prediction_id, signal_id, decision_id, risk_decision_id, execution_intent_id. Every id has a minting module entry (or a P0 GAP entry).\n\n4. Confidence-delta element coverage. The 'Confidence-delta explanation source survey' covers every element REQ_0009 'Confidence explanation' lists: previous confidence, new confidence, delta, contributing feature deltas, positive contributors, negative contributors, source freshness, regime context, model/checkpoint version, data-quality impact.\n\n5. Symbol-state-change element coverage. The 'Symbol-state-change explanation source survey' covers every element REQ_0009 'Symbol selection explanation' lists: source discovery evidence, Binance USD-M confirmation, CoinAnk alias evidence, KuCoin/CoinAPI evidence, liquidity/volume/volatility/open-interest/freshness scores, feature completeness, manual overrides, observed/training/paper/shadow/live-blocked state reason.\n\n6. Risk-decision element coverage. The 'Risk-decision explanation source survey' covers every element REQ_0009 'Trade/risk explanation' lists for the risk side: signal reason, risk gateway result, sizing reason, stale signal check, duplicate check, exposure check, drawdown check, live gate status, execution mode (paper/shadow/live-blocked), final decision reason.\n\n7. Trade-decision element coverage. The 'Trade open/close/hedge/block explanation source survey' covers the open/close/hedge/block transitions and references the corresponding execution and trader modules.\n\n8. Audit-timeline coverage. The 'Audit-timeline source survey' identifies a write-once chain owner (likely v2/backend/app/domain/governance/audit_chain.py if present) or marks a P0 GAP.\n\n9. Gap matrix completeness. All seven tables (A\u2013G) are present in 06. Each gap has a severity (P0/P1/P2) and a proposed owner sub-phase that exists in the Phase 2H breakdown.\n\n10. Cross-cutting concerns. The 'Cross-cutting concerns' section in 06 identifies at least one cross-stage concern (typical example: a missing decision_id minting that affects risk + execution + audit at once). If no concerns are identified, FAIL UNLESS 05 evidence demonstrates none exist.\n\n11. Suggested 2H.A.1 / 2H.A.2 / 2H.A.3 scope. The final section of 06 distills the gap matrix into the three follow-up documentation sub-phases consistent with the Phase 2H breakdown.\n\n12. Forbidden-token grep. Run rg with case-sensitive matching across the entire claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/decision_explainability/ subtree for: redis, aioredis, redis.asyncio, subprocess, os.system, os.popen, pty, socket, urllib, requests, httpx, aiohttp, torch, tensorflow, numpy, cuda, legacy_reference, /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT, BINANCE_API_KEY, BINANCE_API_SECRET, live_trading_enabled = true, XLEN, xlen, time.time(, datetime.now(, datetime.utcnow(. Every count MUST be zero. Any non-zero count is FAIL.\n\n13. END_FILE marker leak check. rg \"^END_FILE:\" claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/decision_explainability/ MUST return zero hits. Any non-zero count is FAIL.\n\n14. No live behavior. Neither 05 nor 06 mentions enabling live trading, mutating legacy, writing Redis, or deploying. The LIVE TRADING: BLOCKED semantics are preserved.\n\n15. Adversarial probes. Try at least: (a) does the inventory accidentally claim ownership for a stage by a module that does not export the cited symbol? (b) does the gap matrix downgrade a P0 audit gap to P2? (c) does any 'GAP' entry quietly imply that legacy code should be imported as the fix? (d) does any proposed-owner sub-phase reference a code package outside v2/backend/app/domain/decision_explanation/?\n\nEmit outputs (BEGIN_FILE / END_FILE blocks \u2014 these are Markdown files and the harness Markdown materialization is safe):\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/decision_explainability/08_2HA0_CODEX_REVIEW.md\n- Heading 'Phase 2H.A.0 \u2014 Codex Review'.\n- One section per rubric item with PASS / FAIL / WARN, evidence pointer (file path and section), and remediation ask if FAIL.\n- Section 'Adversarial coverage probes' listing the additional cases Codex tried and their outcomes.\n- Final marker line: PHASE2HA0_DECISION_LINEAGE_INVENTORY_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2HA0_DECISION_LINEAGE_INVENTORY_CODEX_FAIL.\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/decision_explainability/09_2HA0_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md\n- Exactly one line: PHASE2HA0_DECISION_LINEAGE_INVENTORY_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2HA0_DECISION_LINEAGE_INVENTORY_CODEX_FAIL. No other content.\n\nSafety guarantees. Do not modify any file under v2/. Do not modify legacy. Do not commit. Do not push. Do not run any subprocess other than grep / rg, wc, and python -c for arithmetic. Do not start the legacy trainer venv. Do not import any legacy module. Do not access Redis. Do not access network. Do not read .env. Do not enable live trading. Do not run npm / npx / vite / tsc / playwright / pnpm / yarn / vitest / jest. Do not run pytest. Do not run py_compile.\n\nOn FAIL, the supervisor opens a remediation task under REQ_0007 autofix scope before re-inventory. Codex must NOT silently fix the failure inside this review task.",
