h the matching marker line; preserve the existing wall-clock generated_at and live_gate_status strings. Step 3: Extend v2/backend/tests/unit/proof/test_non_live_operational_proof_artifacts.py test_required_lineage_fields_are_present to require the five new fields. Step 4: Author v2/backend/tests/unit/proof/test_trainer_lineage_parity_fields_coverage.py with three tests per the test plan: (a) decision_explainability_result rows carry the five trainer fields with the per-scenario values, (b) paper_ledger_result events carry the five trainer fields, (c) build_trainer_gate, when invoked against a freshly-written proof artifact, returns marker == TRAINER_LINEAGE_AND_READINESS_READY and gaps == []. Use importlib.util to load the build_autonomous_live_readiness_builder.py module by file path and override its TRAINER and PUBLIC_TRAINER module-level Path constants to tmp_path subdirectories before invoking build_trainer_gate so the test does not write to the production runtime mirror; restore them on teardown. No mock/patch/monkeypatch. Step 5: Run PYTHONPATH=. python3 -m pytest v2/backend/tests/unit/proof -q and capture the result. Step 6: Run PYTHONPATH=. python3 claude_worklog/tools/build_autonomous_live_readiness_builder.py to regenerate the trainer-lineage runtime artifacts under claude_worklog/final_readiness/trainer_lineage_and_readiness/latest/ and v2/frontend/public/trainer_lineage_and_readiness/latest/. Verify the regenerated GO_NO_GO.md files contain exactly TRAINER_LINEAGE_AND_READINESS_READY and that trainer_lineage_coverage.json has gaps == []. Step 7: Author claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_lineage_parity_fields_extension/06_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md summarizing files edited, fixture values used, pytest output, builder output, and marker flip evidence. Step 8: Author claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_lineage_parity_fields_extension/07_GO_NO_GO.md containing exactly one line: PHASE2V_TRAINER_LINEAGE_PARITY_FIELDS_EXTENSION_READY_FOR_CODEX_REVIEW. Output every authored file via BEGIN_FILE / END_FILE blocks pointing at the exact paths in required_output_files. Do not output any standalone END_FILE marker line in any authored file body."
