laude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/49_2E1C_ALPHA_VALIDATION_RUN_LOG.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/69_CODEX_PARALLEL_REVIEW_TRAINER_LIVENESS.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/71_CODEX_PARALLEL_TRAINER_LIVENESS_AUTOFIX_REPORT.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/73_CODEX_PARALLEL_REREVIEW_TRAINER_LIVENESS_AUTOFIX.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/75_PLANNER_2E1C_ALPHA_TASK_DEFINITION_REFRESH_NOTE.md\n- v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness/ (all 6 source files)\n- v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness/ (all 12 test files including test_evaluator_prediction_worker_dead.py)\n\nReview rubric. For each rubric item, record PASS / FAIL / WARN with evidence pointers (file path and line range).\n\n1. Public surface integrity. __all__ is exactly the 11 names declared in the post-autofix spec: LivenessSignalSnapshot, LivenessSLAConfig, LivenessAlert, evaluate_liveness, LivenessDomainError, LIVENESS_REASON_PREDICTION_AGE_EXCEEDS_SLA, LIVENESS_REASON_GPU_BATCH_AGE_EXCEEDS_SLA, LIVENESS_REASON_PROPOSAL_AGE_EXCEEDS_SLA, LIVENESS_REASON_PREDICTION_STREAM_ZERO_GROWTH, LIVENESS_REASON_PREDICTION_WORKER_DEAD, LIVENESS_REASON_FATAL_LOG_SIGNATURE_OBSERVED. LIVENESS_ALERT_CODE is NOT in __all__. errors submodule is NOT in __all__. No 2E1.B name leaked.\n\n2. Spec faithfulness - LivenessSignalSnapshot. Field set, ordering, types, and __post_init__ invariants exactly match spec 42. Negative-value rejection coverage is complete. The bool-typed prediction_worker_alive and fatal_log_signature_observed fields are strictly bool-typed (isinstance(bool) checks). The trainer_rss_bytes-requires-trainer_pid and prediction_worker_alive-requires-prediction_worker_pid invariants are enforced.\n\n3. Spec faithfulness - LivenessSLAConfig. Same as #2 for the SLA fields.\n\n4. Spec faithfulness - LivenessAlert and reason constants. alert_code constraint enforced. _ALLOWED_LIVENESS_REASONS contains exactly six reasons: prediction_age_exceeds_sla, gpu_batch_age_exceeds_sla, proposal_age_exceeds_sla, prediction_stream_zero_growth, prediction_worker_dead, fatal_log_signature_observed. Unknown / duplicate / empty reasons rejected. observation_ts_ms == snapshot.observation_ts_ms enforced.\n\n5. Spec faithfulness - evaluator (post-autofix six-rule version). The six rules are implemented in this exact evaluation order: prediction_age_exceeds_sla, gpu_batch_age_exceeds_sla, proposal_age_exceeds_sla, prediction_stream_zero_growth, prediction_worker_dead, fatal_log_signature_observed. The prediction_worker_dead rule is evaluated INDEPENDENTLY of the zero-stream-growth branch (a non-zero prediction_stream_id_growth must NOT suppress the worker-dead alert; verify by re-reading evaluator.py:48-57 and the targeted test test_evaluator_prediction_worker_dead.py). None-handling for missing timestamps (never-emitted case) is correct: prediction-age reason does NOT fire when last_prediction_ts_ms is None; the zero-stream-growth reason still covers the never-emitted case when parent is alive. Strict > comparison for SLA boundaries (equal-to-SLA returns None). now_ms < observation_ts_ms raises. now_ms < 0 raises. Returns None when no reasons fire. Returns LivenessAlert with deterministic reason ordering otherwise.\n\n6. Out-of-band requirement compliance per 05 spec. No write to legacy Redis (verified by grep). No restart of the legacy trainer (no subprocess calls, no os.kill, no process management). No XLEN-style growth measurement (the field name is prediction_stream_id_growth and the evaluator treats it as already-measured-over-window; the consumption order matches the timezone-aware corrected approach). No emission to V2_REDIS_PREFIX in this phase.\n\n7. Hard-exclusion compliance. No subprocess. No file I/O. No network. No Redis. No legacy import. No environment variable read. No reliance on the 2E1.A subprocess adapter. No live trainer call. No model / checkpoint loading. No GPU code. No async. No clock read. No numpy. No torch. No tensorflow. Verify by re-running the forbidden-token grep over the trainer_liveness source and test trees.\n\n8. END_FILE marker hygiene. rg \"^END_FILE:\" returns zero hits across both source and test trees. py_compile succeeds for all 18 Python files (re-run via Bash; do not modify any file).\n\n9. Test coverage. Each rubric in spec 43 maps to at least one test. Specifically confirm presence of test_evaluator_prediction_worker_dead.py with at least the autofix-introduced case proving worker-dead alerts even when prediction_stream_id_growth is non-zero. Note any missing case (especially equal-to-SLA boundary, never-emitted prediction, RSS-None-with-parent-alive treated as parent-not-alive, deterministic reason ordering across permutations of trigger inputs, multi-reason ordering when worker_dead fires alongside zero-growth and fatal-log).\n\n10. Cross-symbol isolation. trainer_liveness must not import any symbol from v2.backend.app.domain.trainer_parity. trainer_parity must remain unmodified. The autofix must not have leaked any liveness symbol into trainer_parity.\n\n11. Documentation alignment. Field rationales documented inline (e.g. why deconflict freshness is captured but not consulted by alpha; why None timestamps do not trigger age reasons; why prediction_worker_dead is independent of zero_growth). Implementation report (47) and the autofix report (71) and re-review (73) accurately reflect authored state.\n\n12. Safety boundaries adherence. Spec 44 forbidden-action list is fully respected. No live trading enablement. LIVE TRADING: BLOCKED is preserved. The autofix did not introduce any new external dependency, subprocess, or Redis path.\n\nEmit outputs (BEGIN_FILE / END_FILE blocks - these are Markdown files):\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/50_2E1C_ALPHA_CODEX_REVIEW.md\n- Heading 'Phase 2E1.C.alpha - Codex Review (revision 2, post-autofix)'.\n- One section per rubric item with PASS / FAIL / WARN, evidence pointer (file path and line range or marker), and remediation ask if FAIL.\n- Section 'Adversarial coverage probes' listing any additional cases Codex tried that are not in spec 43 (e.g. snapshot with all timestamps in the future, evaluator with snapshot.observation_ts_ms == 0, worker-dead concurrent with all five other reasons).\n- Section 'Autofix continuity check' confirming that the post-autofix evaluator and tests still satisfy every rubric that the pre-autofix code already satisfied (no regression).\n- Final marker line: PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_FAIL.\n\nclaude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/51_2E1C_ALPHA_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md\n- Exactly one line: PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS or PHASE2E1C_ALPHA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_FAIL. No other content.\n\nSafety guarantees. Do not modify any file under v2/backend/. Do not modify legacy. Do not commit. Do not push. Do not run any subprocess other than pytest (read-only re-run is allowed for verification), python -m py_compile, python -c, and grep / rg. Do not start the legacy trainer venv. Do not import any legacy module. Do not access Redis. Do not access network. Do not read .env. Do not enable live trading.\n\nOn FAIL, the supervisor opens a remediation task under REQ_0007 autofix scope before re-implementation. Codex must NOT silently fix the failure inside this review task.",
