es via __all__ in the documented order; no extras; no submodule re-exports; no _ -prefixed leaks; no re-export of alpha, beta, or delta public symbols.\n2. ObservationCollectorError matches spec 88 (constructor signature, __str__ behavior, no inheritance from alpha, beta, or delta error types).\n3. StreamLatestIdReader is a typing.Protocol decorated with @runtime_checkable; it declares exactly latest_stream_id(self, stream_name: str) -> str | None; reader_protocol.py does NOT import any Redis client.\n4. InMemoryStreamLatestIdReader.__init__ rejects non-dict, non-str keys, and non-(str-or-None) values with ObservationCollectorError; stores a defensive copy via dict(...).\n5. InMemoryStreamLatestIdReader.latest_stream_id rejects non-str or empty stream_name with ObservationCollectorError, otherwise returns the configured value (or None).\n6. InMemoryStreamLatestIdReader satisfies isinstance(reader, StreamLatestIdReader) at runtime.\n7. collect_stream_id_observations executes the nine-step behavior contract from spec 88 in the exact documented order. Each step is reachable and tested.\n8. The collector calls clock_ms exactly once per invocation; every observation produced shares the same observation_ts_ms.\n9. The collector skips streams whose reader returns None and does not raise.\n10. The collector propagates beta LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError unchanged when a returned stream_id fails beta StreamIdObservation construction.\n11. The collector does NOT mutate reader, stream_names, or any beta-owned object.\n12. extend_observation_history executes the nine-step behavior contract from spec 88 in the exact documented order. Each step is reachable and tested.\n13. extend_observation_history truncates from the FRONT (drops oldest) when len(combined) > max_total.\n14. extend_observation_history does NOT mutate history or new.\n15. Forbidden-token grep across gamma source and test trees returns zero per the canonical list in spec 89.\n16. END_FILE marker leak self-check returns zero across the four narrow scopes from spec 89: gamma source tree, gamma test tree, file 92, file 93. Do NOT widen the grep to the full trainer_gpu_parity_impl/ tree; older planner directives in that tree are out of scope.\n17. test_forbidden_tokens references each forbidden token via runtime-fragment concatenation so that the grep over the test tree returns zero for each token.\n18. Cross-isolation: alpha, beta, AND delta source trees are unmodified (git status -s returns zero lines for all three) and alpha/beta/delta pytest suites pass after gamma is added.\n19. No Redis client, subprocess, network, clock, or legacy import anywhere in the gamma source or test trees.\n20. No write to v2/backend/app/adapters/, v2/backend/app/services/, v2/backend/app/api/, v2/backend/app/cli/, v2/backend/app/jobs/, v2/backend/app/main.py, or v2/frontend/.\n21. No secret-shaped string in the diff.\n22. py_compile passes for every authored Python file.\n23. Gamma pytest suite passes with zero failures and zero errors.\n\nValidation commands you MAY run (read-only):\n- .venv/bin/python -m pytest v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/ -q\n- .venv/bin/python -m pytest v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness/ v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/ v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_composition/ -q\n- python -m py_compile <each authored .py file>\n- rg --fixed-strings --case-sensitive <forbidden token> v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/ v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/\n- rg \"^END_FILE:\" v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/\n- rg \"^END_FILE:\" v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/\n- rg \"^END_FILE:\" claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/92_2E1C_GAMMA_GO_NO_GO.md\n- rg \"^END_FILE:\" claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/93_2E1C_GAMMA_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md\n- git status -s v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness/ v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/ v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness_composition/\n\nEmit 94_2E1C_GAMMA_CODEX_REVIEW.md with sections: 'Files reviewed' (list with line ranges), 'Rubric findings' (one row per rubric item 1-23 with PASS/FAIL + cited evidence), 'Validation commands run' (each command with exit code and summary line), 'Concrete blockers' (zero rows on PASS; otherwise enumerate), 'Safety review' (live behavior, Redis writes, Redis client imports, legacy mutation, deployment intent, secret-shaped strings — each must be 'none observed' to PASS), 'Recommendation' (PASS or FAIL). Final marker: PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_CODEX_REVIEW_READY. The file MUST NOT contain any END_FILE marker line in its body.\n\nEmit 95_2E1C_GAMMA_CODEX_GO_NO_GO.md. Exactly one of:\n  PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_PASS\n  PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_CODEX_FAIL\nNo other content. The file MUST NOT contain any END_FILE marker line.\n\nIf you find concrete non-live blockers, do NOT autofix them in this task. Instead emit FAIL with a precise blocker enumeration in 94 'Concrete blockers'. The supervisor will dispatch a separate REQ_0007/REQ_0014 autofix task that is allowed to patch v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/ and v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/ only. The autofix task is not allowed to touch alpha, beta, or delta packages.\n\nStop conditions: any live behavior, any Redis client import (even unused), any Redis write, any legacy mutation, any deployment intent, or any secret leakage in the gamma diff is an unconditional FAIL with no autofix path; surface to human attention.",
