claude_worklog/planner_recovery/paper_ledger_2hb_stale_fail/2HB_MARKER_SEARCH.txt:6455:claude_worklog/agent_supervisor/runs/086A_trainer_parity_2e1c_gamma_reader_protocol/stderr.txt:8273:  "prompt": "You are local Claude in /home/wali/Desktop/AI BOT REBUILD acting as the Phase 2E1.C.gamma implementer for REQ_0006 (V2 trainer GPU parity service). You author the trainer-liveness STREAM-ID OBSERVATION COLLECTOR DOMAIN LAYER ONLY. You do not modify legacy. You do not run the live trainer. You do not write Redis. You do not read Redis. You do not import any Redis client. You do not place exchange orders. You do not deploy. You do not expose or commit secrets. You do not commit or push.\n\nThis task is a Max20 consolidated milestone task. Implementation, forbidden-token self-grep, END_FILE leak self-check, py_compile, pytest, alpha/beta/delta cross-isolation regression, and status-report authoring are ALL performed in this single task. Do not request a split into sub-tasks unless this task fails for an emit/path/size/timeout reason.\n\nRead exactly these files first as authoritative:\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/88_PHASE_2E1C_GAMMA_OBSERVATION_COLLECTOR_SPEC.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/89_PHASE_2E1C_GAMMA_TEST_PLAN.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/90_PHASE_2E1C_GAMMA_SAFETY_BOUNDARIES.md\n- claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/91_PHASE_2E1C_GAMMA_GO_NO_GO_REQUEST.md\n- v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/__init__.py (read-only; beta public surface)\n- v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/stream_observation.py (read-only; StreamIdObservation contract)\n- v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/errors.py (read-only; LivenessStreamGrowthDomainError contract)\n\nAuthor exactly the files listed in required_output_files and no others. The six Python source files and twenty-nine Python test files (plus the package marker) are pure-Python, sync, no-async, no-Redis, no-subprocess, no-network, no-clock, no-legacy. The two Markdown files are status reports.\n\nStep 1 - author the package files per spec 88 'Surface to create' and 'Public surface'. The __init__.py must export exactly the five names declared in spec 88 in the documented order via __all__. errors.py defines ObservationCollectorError per spec 88 'ObservationCollectorError' section. reader_protocol.py defines StreamLatestIdReader per spec 88 'StreamLatestIdReader' section using typing.Protocol with @runtime_checkable. in_memory_reader.py defines InMemoryStreamLatestIdReader per spec 88 'InMemoryStreamLatestIdReader' section. observation_collector.py defines collect_stream_id_observations per spec 88 'collect_stream_id_observations' section, executing the nine-step behavior contract in the exact order documented. observation_history.py defines extend_observation_history per spec 88 'extend_observation_history' section, executing the nine-step behavior contract in the exact order documented.\n\nStep 2 - author the test files per spec 89. Each rubric in spec 89 'Required rubric coverage' must map to at least one test case; provide one test function per rubric row. Use only stdlib + pytest + the gamma public surface + the beta public surface. test_forbidden_tokens.py MUST use pure-Python pathlib walks and runtime-fragment-concatenation for the forbidden tokens themselves so that grep over the test tree returns zero hits per token.\n\nStep 3 - run a self-grep for the forbidden tokens listed in spec 89 'Forbidden-token grep (canonical list)' across the gamma source AND test trees. Use rg with case-sensitive fixed-string matching. Record the per-token raw counts. Every count MUST be zero. Any non-zero count is a hard fail and you MUST emit PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_BLOCKED to 92_2E1C_GAMMA_GO_NO_GO.md and stop.\n\nStep 4 - run rg \"^END_FILE:\" against the four narrow scopes specified in spec 89 'END_FILE marker leak self-check': (a) the gamma source tree v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/, (b) the gamma test tree v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/, (c) the implementer-authored file claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/92_2E1C_GAMMA_GO_NO_GO.md, (d) the implementer-authored file claude_worklog/phase2_core_rebuild/trainer_gpu_parity_impl/93_2E1C_GAMMA_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md. All four counts MUST be zero. Any non-zero hit in any of the four scopes is a hard fail and you MUST emit PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_BLOCKED. Do NOT widen the grep to the full trainer_gpu_parity_impl/ tree; older committed planner directives in that tree may legitimately contain END_FILE markers from prior planner-emit format and are out of scope for this sub-phase.\n\nStep 5 - run python -m py_compile against every authored Python file. Any failure is a hard fail.\n\nStep 6 - run pytest against the gamma tests directory using .venv/bin/python. Capture stdout/stderr verbatim. Command: .venv/bin/python -m pytest v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_observation_collector/ -q. The summary line MUST show zero failures and zero errors. Any failure or error is a hard fail.\n\nStep 7 - run cross-isolation regression: .venv/bin/python -m pytest v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness/ v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/liveness_stream_growth/ v2/backend/tests/unit/domain/trainer_liveness_composition/ -q. All three suites (alpha, beta, delta) MUST remain green. Any failure or error is a hard fail. Then run git status -s v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness/ v2/backend/app/domain/liveness_stream_growth/ v2/backend/app/domain/trainer_liveness_composition/ and confirm zero modified lines. Any modified line is a hard fail.\n\nStep 8 - emit 92_2E1C_GAMMA_GO_NO_GO.md. Exactly one of:\n  PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_AND_VALIDATION_PASSED\n  PHASE2E1C_GAMMA_TRAINER_PARITY_IMPL_BLOCKED\nNo other content. The file MUST NOT contain any E